From: mscharged-port
Subject: Blur the picture in the window behind a host panel
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host presentation (host panel). Apply after 0120.

A host panel over the game (the online panel F1 or HOME opens) sits on a
frosted picture: the game goes on, blurred, behind it. The host darkens the
picture with its overlay; this patch blurs it.

aurora_set_video_output_blur(true) blurs the window's picture from the next
present: the shown desktop picture (after FXAA, when on) is reduced to about
270 rows, each pixel the average of the block it covers, then blurred across
and down with a Gaussian of 5 of those rows (three small render passes, a few
hundred thousand pixels each), and drawn scaled up into the same viewport.
false shows it sharp again. Screenshots keep using the sharp picture's bind
group, the EFB, XFB and the game's frames are untouched, and the host overlay
is drawn over the blurred picture as before.

